each the slab and the baseboards. Extraction focuses on edges, doorways and transitions.","l":[]},{"t":"h3","x":"Hardwood and Engineered Wood"},{"t":"p","x":"Wood starts to cup within hours. Fast extraction plus specialty floor-drying mats give the best chance of saving it.","l":[]},{"t":"h3","x":"Bare Concrete and Garages"},{"t":"p","x":"Garages flood often from water heaters and washers. Squeegees, pumps and air movers clear them quickly so water does not spread into the house.","l":[]},{"t":"h2","x":"Flooded Floor Cleanup: What You Can Do Before We Arrive"},{"t":"p","x":"While the crew is on the way, these steps help limit damage without putting you at risk:","l":[]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"x":"Shut off the main water valve. On many Apopka homes it is near the front hose bib or inside the garage.","l":[]},{"x":"Turn off breakers for any room where water touches outlets, power strips or cords.","l":[]},{"x":"Take photos and video for your insurance claim before moving anything.","l":[]},{"x":"Lift wooden furniture onto foil squares or blocks to stop stains and swelling.","l":[]},{"x":"Move rugs, paperwork, shoes and electronics to a dry room.","l":[]},{"x":"Keep children and pets out of the wet area.","l":[]},{"x":"Do not run a household vacuum on standing water, and do not walk through water that may be sewage.","l":[]}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Signs Extraction Was Not Enough"},{"t":"p","x":"If water was mopped or wet-vacuumed but not professionally extracted, watch for these over the next few days:","l":[]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"x":"A musty smell that gets stronger instead of fading.","l":[]},{"x":"Baseboards that swell, crack or pull away from the wall.","l":[]},{"x":"Carpet that stays damp or smells sour after 24 hours.","l":[]},{"x":"LVP planks that lift, gap or feel soft.","l":[]},{"x":"Bubbling or peeling paint along the bottom of walls.","l":[]},{"x":"Any of these mean water is still in the structure. A moisture check and proper structural drying is the next step. Rea