er and every affected room.","l":[]},{"x":"Move furniture, electronics, rugs and paperwork out of the water.","l":[]},{"x":"Put towels at doorways to slow the spread into dry rooms.","l":[]},{"x":"Call (407) 787-9139 so a crew is dispatched immediately.","l":[]},{"x":"Do not try to cut into drywall to find the leak yourself. Ceiling drywall full of water is heavy and can come down without warning.","l":[]}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Why Pipes Burst in Apopka Homes"},{"t":"p","x":"Florida rarely freezes, so most burst pipes here have other causes. Knowing the cause helps us dry the right areas and helps you prevent the next one.","l":[]},{"t":"h3","x":"Aging Supply Lines in Established Neighborhoods"},{"t":"p","x":"Homes built from the 1970s through the 1990s around Errol Estate, downtown and the Park Avenue area may still have original copper, CPVC or even polybutylene lines. Polybutylene, the gray plastic pipe common in that era, becomes brittle and splits at fittings. CPVC grows brittle with heat and age, especially in hot attics.","l":[]},{"t":"h3","x":"Pinhole Leaks in Copper"},{"t":"p","x":"Water chemistry and age cause copper to develop tiny pinholes that spray inside walls for days before anyone notices.","l":[]},{"t":"h3","x":"Failed Fittings and Braided Supply Lines"},{"t":"p","x":"Toilet, sink and appliance supply lines with plastic nuts crack under pressure. A single failed line under a vanity can flood a bathroom and the hallway outside it.","l":[]},{"t":"h3","x":"High Water Pressure"},{"t":"p","x":"Without a working pressure-reducing valve, pressure spikes stress every joint in the house.","l":[]},{"t":"h3","x":"Attic Pipe Runs"},{"t":"p","x":"Many Florida homes run water lines through the attic. When one fails, water comes straight through the ceiling into the rooms below.","l":[]},{"t":"h3","x":"Lines Under the Slab"},{"t":"p","x":"When a pipe fails under the concrete, the water shows up as damp flooring or a warm spot rather than a spray. Read more: Slab Leak 